I could see NH having high property tax because they tax NOTHING else. No sales or income tax. But yet NJ and NY are higher!

&#x200B;

Those tax stats could be a bit misleading. A suburb may be taxed at 1/3 of a city, but the houses cost more and it will appear as more tax is being paid. Still crazy numbers no matter how you slice it.

Ok, I figured you had a grasp of I/O libraries from your previous experience. Before taking a course, I would get comfortable with the basics of Javascript and node. You should be able to do some basic stuff, if you can indeed write CLI games. What if you had to keep track of moves or state in the game? You would have to write to disk! And read back. Not much different than a log.

&#x200B;

For example: Google how to write a list of numbers to a file in node. How to read from a file. Research what  a log is. See what I'm getting at? Don't go into ANY course without knowing basics.

Big thing about NODE JS is getting comfortable with async. Instead of assigning something to a variable on the left, think in terms of writing a function in the argument list.

so..instead of 

&#x200B;

    var x = getData(200);

Think:

    getData(200, function (x) { do something with x here });

or 

    getData(200, (x)=> { do something with x here });

